cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "kids-chd: A Shiny web application for calculating CPET endpoints for children with congenital heart defects"
authors:
  - family-names: Leoncio
    given-names: Waldir
    email: w.l.netto@medisin.uio.no
    affiliation: "Oslo Centre for Biostatistics and Epidemiology (OCBE), University of Oslo"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ocbe-uio/kids-chd"
license: GPL-3.0
version: 0.0.0.9038
abstract: "A Shiny web application for calculating cardiopulmonary exercise test (CPET) endpoints for children with congenital heart defects. The application provides predicted cardiopulmonary endpoints (VO2, heart rate, ventilation, oxygen pulse, VE/VCO2 slope, and breathing frequency) based on diagnostic group, height, and BMI, with confidence intervals."
keywords:
  - "congenital heart defects"
  - "CPET"
  - "cardiopulmonary exercise test"
  - "Shiny"
  - "R"
  - "pediatrics"
